c as each character gets processed through the multiplication and addition steps. Continuing through characters 'a', 's', 't', 'e', 'r' with the same modular arithmetic pattern, applying multiplications by 33, adding character codes, and reducing by powers of 2^32 to keep values in range, which gives me 2112778853 as the final hash value before converting to hexadecimal. Finishing the division to get the remaining hex digits, then verifying the complete conversion: 0x7DEE7265 equals 2112778853 when I work through each hex place value. The hash is HDLmClass7.\n\nNow I'm building out a full HTML page with a header, navigation bar using that class, a hero section, featured products area, some about text, and a footer.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":1,"signature":""}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":4021,"completion_tokens":9501,"total_tokens":13522,"cost":0.25763,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.25763,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.020105,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.237525},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":465,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0},"server_tool_use_details":{"web_search_requests":0}}}
