v class=\\\"bulk-copy\\\">\\n      <h2>Bulk &amp; Wholesale Orders</h2>\\n      <p>Outfitting a studio, gym, school, hotel, retreat or corporate event? Because we manufacture and source our own goods, we can quote volume pricing other suppliers can't match.</p>\\n      <div class=\\\"tiers\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"tier\\\"><b>10+</b>Save 10%</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"tier\\\"><b>25+</b>Save 15%</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"tier\\\"><b>50+</b>Save 20%</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"tier\\\"><b>100+</b>Save 25%+</div>\\n      </div>\\n      <ul>\\n        <li>Dedicated bulk specialist &mdash; one contact from quote to delivery</li>\\n        <li>Quotes answered within 1 business day</li>\\n        <li>Freight shipping, split shipments and PO / net terms available</li>\\n        <li>Custom logo printing on mats and bags</li>\\n      </ul>\\n      <p><strong>Prefer to talk?</strong> Call <a href=\\\"tel:18005559642\\\" style=\\\"color:#fff;text-decoration:underline\\\">1-800-555-YOGA</a> or email <a href=\\\"mailto:bulk@yogadirect.com\\\" style=\\\"color:#fff;text-decoration:underline\\\">bulk@yogadirect.com</a>.</p>\\n    </div>\\n    <form class=\\\"bulk-form\\\" action=\\\"/bulk-quote/\\\" method=\\\"post\\\">\\n      <h3>Get your bulk quote</h3>\\n      <p class=\\\"small\\\">Takes 30 seconds. No obligation, no account needed.</p>\\n      <label for=\\\"bq-name\\\">Name</label>\\n      <input id=\\\"bq-name\\\" name=\\\"name\\\" type=\\\"text\\\" required>\\n      <label for=\\\"bq-email\\\">Email</label>\\n      <input id=\\\"bq-email\\\" name=\\\"email\\\" type=\\\"email\\\" required>\\n      <label for=\\\"bq-org\\\">Studio / Organization</label>\\n      <input id=\\\"bq-org\\\" name=\\\"organization\\\" type=\\\"text\\\">\\n      <label for=\\\"bq-qty\\\">Estimated quantity</label>\\n      <select id=\\\"bq-qty\\\" name=\\\"quantity\\\">\\n        <option>10 &ndash; 24 units</option>\\n        <option>25 &ndash; 49 units</option>\\n        <option>50 &ndash; 99 units</option>\\n        <option>100+ units</option>\\n      </select>\\n      <label for=\\\"bq-items\\\">What do you need?</label>\\n      <textarea id=\\\"bq-items\\\" name=\\\"items\\\" rows=\\\"3\\\" placeholder=\\\"e.g. 40 deluxe mats, 40 blocks, 20 straps\\\"></textarea>\\n      <button class=\\\"btn btn-bulk\\\" type=\\\"submit\\\">Send My Bulk Quote Request</button>\\n      <p class=\\\"reassure\\\">We reply within 1 business day. Your details are never shared.</p>\\n    </form>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\\n<section class=\\\"about\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <h2 style=\\\"text-align:center\\\">Supplying the yoga community since 1999</h2>\\n    <p>Thanks to our loyal customers, YogaDirect has become one of the largest suppliers of yoga mats and props in the country. We have been faithfully supplying the Yoga community since 1999 and are confident that we can help you grow your studio, event, or personal practice with everything you need and more. We manufacture and source our own goods which is how we can consistently offer high-quality yoga gear at amazing prices. When you shop at YogaDirect, feel proud in knowing that you are helping to grow not only your business or personal practice but the Yoga community as a whole. From our team of Yoga lovers to you, thank you.</p>\\n    <p style=\\\"text-align:center;margin-top:20px\\\"><a class=\\\"btn btn-bulk HDLmClassebef7055\\\" href=\\\"#bulk-order\\\">Outfitting a studio? Get bulk pricing</a></p>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\\n<footer>\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <div class=\\\"footer-bulk HDLmClassb727f92a\\\">\\n      <div>\\n        <h3>Ordering for a studio, school or event?</h3>\\n        <p>Volume discounts from 10 units, custom logo printing and freight shipping available.</p>\\n      </div>\\n      <a class=\\\"btn btn-bulk\\\" href=\\\"#bulk-order\\\">Request a Bulk Order Quote</a>\\n    </div>\\n    <div class=\\\"fgrid\\\">\\n      <div>\\n        <h4>Shop</h4>\\n        <ul>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/yoga-mats/\\\">Yoga Mats</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/yoga-blocks/\\\">Blocks &amp; Wedges</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/bolsters/\\\">Bolsters</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/sale/\\\">Sale</a></li>\\n        </ul>\\n      </div>\\n      <div>\\n        <h4>Wholesale</h4>\\n        <ul>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"#bulk-order\\\" class=\\\"HDLmClassb727f92a\\\">Bulk Order Quote</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"#bulk-order\\\" class=\\\"HDLmClassb727f92a\\\">Volume Discount Tiers</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"#bulk-order\\\">Studio &amp; School Programs</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"#bulk-order\\\">Custom Logo Printing</a></li>\\n        </ul>\\n      </div>\\n      <div>\\n        <h4>Help</h4>\\n        <ul>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/shipping-returns/\\\">Shipping &amp; Returns</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/contact-us/\\\">Contact Us</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/faq/\\\">FAQ</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/login.php\\\">My Account</a></li>\\n        </ul>\\n      </div>\\n      <div>\\n        <h4>Contact</h4>\\n        <ul>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"tel:18005559642\\\">1-800-555-YOGA</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"mailto:bulk@yogadirect.com\\\">bulk@yogadirect.com</a></li>\\n          <li>Mon&ndash;Fri, 9am&ndash;5pm ET</li>\\n        </ul>\\n      </div>\\n    </div>\\n    <div class=\\\"copy\\\">&copy; YogaDirect. All rights reserved.</div>\\n  </div>\\n</footer>\\n\\n</body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Added a bulk order CTA button in the header\",\"Why\":\"Bulk buyers have higher order values and need a fast path to quotes\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClassebef7055\"},{\"What\":\"Added a bulk order quote section\",\"Why\":\"Volume discount tiers push studios to buy more\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClassacb6047e\"},{\"What\":\"Added a bulk order CTA to the footer\",\"Why\":\"Captures wholesale buyers who scroll to the end\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClassb727f92a\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I need to build out the HTML structure for the YogaDirect homepage since the fetch only gave me text. I'll create a complete page that incorporates bulk order CTAs in key places like the hero banner and sticky navigation to showcase the desired changes.\n\nNow I'm computing DJB2 hashes for the improvements. For the first one, I'm hashing the concatenated \"What\" and \"Why\" strings together to create a unique identifier for this specific change. Continuing through the character codes for the rest of the string...\n\nNow I'm working through a hash calculation using a specific algorithm, starting with an initial value and iteratively multiplying by 33 while adding each character's ASCII value. Continuing with 'a': multiplying by 33, adding the character code, and taking modulo 2^32 gives 2144832472. Then for the space character, I'm applying the same hash function steps to get 2059994872. Finally, for 'b', I'm computing the hash value through multiplication, addition, and modular arithmetic, which yields 3555321. Continuing through the hash computation for each character in the string, tracking the modular arithmetic operations and intermediate values as I process 'o', 'r', 'd', 'e', and the start of another 'r'. Continuing through the hash computation for characters 22-25, tracking the modular arithmetic and differences as each character gets processed. Continuing through the hash computation for each character—working through 'i', 'n', space, and 't', calculating the rolling hash values and differences at each step. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters, tracking the multiplied values, remainders, and differences at each step. Continuing the hash computation through characters 'k', space, 'b', 'u', and 'y', tracking the rolling hash values and differences at each step. Continuing through the character sequence, processing 'h', 'a', 'v', 'e' with their respective ASCII values and computing the running differences through the multiplication and addition operations. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters, working through the multiplications and modular arithmetic to track the running difference values as each character gets processed. Continuing through the character sequence, computing hash values for 'r', space, 'v', and 'a' with their respective multiplications and differences tracked at each step. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters, working through the space, 'a', 'n', and 'd' with their respective multiplications and difference calculations. Continuing through the hash computation iterations, working through characters and their contributions to the running total with the multiplication and addition operations. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters in \"path\", tracking the multiplications and differences at each step. Computing hash values for the remaining characters in \"quote\"—working through each character's polynomial rolling hash calculation with the multiply-by-33, shift-by-32 operations, and tracking the differences at each step. Continuing the hex conversion by working through each digit position, I get ebef7055, which I verify by converting back to decimal and confirming it matches the original value of 3958337621. Hash1 is now HDLm.\n\nFor the second improvement, I'm refining the description of a bulk order quote section with volume discount tiers. The initial concatenation is too long at around 145 characters, so I'm trimming it down to focus on the key benefit: that volume discounts encourage studios to place larger orders. Continuing through the hash computation for each character, tracking the rolling hash value and differences as I process \"quote section\" and beyond. Continuing through the character sequence, computing hash values for 't', 'i', 'o', 'n', and starting on 'V' with the rolling hash algorithm. Continuing through the character processing with the same hash computation pattern, working through 'e', space, 'd', and into 'i'. Continuing through characters 46-50, computing hash values with modular arithmetic for 'n', 't', space, 't', and 'i', tracking the differences after each subtraction of powers of 2. Continuing through the character processing with the hash calculations, working through space, 'p', 'u', 's', and 'h' characters with their respective multiplications and difference computations. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters—'u', 'd', 'i', 'o', 's'—applying the same multiplication and modulo operations to track the rolling hash values and their differences at each step. Continuing through the character processing with the rolling hash calculations, tracking the differences between expected and computed values for each character in the sequence. I'm converting the remainder into hex digits by dividing by powers of 16, getting the sequence A C B 6 0 4 7 E, which reconstructs to the hash value 2897609854 when verified. The final hash is \"HDLmClassacb6047e\".\n\nNow I'm thinking through a third improvement to add alongside the bulk order CTA—maybe a trust or benefit line, but I should keep it focused. I'll go with adding a bulk order CTA banner at the top of the page as a site-wide bar for the third improvement. Computing hash values through the string... Continuing through the character sequence, processing 'o', 't', 'e', 'r', and 'C' with the same multiplication and modulo operations to track the running differences. Continuing through the character sequence, computing hash values and differences for 'r', 'e', 's', and the space character. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters, working through 'e', 's', 'a', 'l', and starting on the final 'e', applying the same multiplication and modulo operations at each step. Continuing through the hash computation for each character in \"buyers\", tracking the intermediate values and differences as I process 'e', 'r', 's', and the space character. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters, working through 's', 'c', 'r', 'o', and 'l' with their respective ASCII values and intermediate calculations. Continuing through the character sequence, processing each character's hash value through the same multiplication and modulo operations to track the running differences. Converting the hash value to hexadecimal by repeatedly dividing by powers of 16 and collecting the remainders, which gives me \"b727f92a\", then verifying the conversion by expanding each hex digit back to decimal to confirm it matches the original value.\n\nNow I'm reconstructing a complete YogaDirect homepage in HTML with the featured products section, navigation, about text, and bulk order call-to-action buttons that use the hash class, keeping it as a single-line JSON structure.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I need to build out the HTML structure for the YogaDirect homepage since the fetch only gave me text. I'll create a complete page that incorporates bulk order CTAs in key places like the hero banner and sticky navigation to showcase the desired changes.\n\nNow I'm computing DJB2 hashes for the improvements. For the first one, I'm hashing the concatenated \"What\" and \"Why\" strings together to create a unique identifier for this specific change. Continuing through the character codes for the rest of the string...\n\nNow I'm working through a hash calculation using a specific algorithm, starting with an initial value and iteratively multiplying by 33 while adding each character's ASCII value. Continuing with 'a': multiplying by 33, adding the character code, and taking modulo 2^32 gives 2144832472. Then for the space character, I'm applying the same hash function steps to get 2059994872. Finally, for 'b', I'm computing the hash value through multiplication, addition, and modular arithmetic, which yields 3555321. Continuing through the hash com