ning characters of \"Shop a\" by applying the same polynomial rolling hash algorithm with modular arithmetic. Continuing through the hash calculations for the remaining characters in \"link\", then moving on to analyze the \"Why\" string about promotional strategies and their impact on conversion metrics. Continuing the hash calculations through the remaining characters of \"promotion\" to verify the final hash value. Continuing the hash computation through the remaining characters of \"banner s\", processing each letter through the polynomial rolling hash algorithm with modular arithmetic to track the intermediate values. Continuing the hash calculations through the remaining characters of the string. Computing the hash value for the space character and continuing through the remaining characters, accounting for the 32-bit overflow when the intermediate result exceeds the maximum value. Continuing the hash computation through the remaining characters of the string, processing each letter and applying the modulo operations to keep the values within bounds. Continuing to work through the hash computation, I'm verifying each character's contribution to the running hash value, carefully handling the modulo arithmetic to keep the values in range. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters in \"increaseS\" — working through each letter with the rolling hash algorithm, applying modulo operations to keep values within bounds. Continuing the hash calculations... Continuing the hash computation... Continuing the hash computation... Continuing the hash computation... Continuing the hash computation through the remaining characters of \"hates by cr\"... Computing hash values... Continuing through the hash calculations for the remaining characters in \"and ince\"... Continuing the hash computation... I need to recalculate that last step—I made an error with the modulo arithmetic. Let me redo it: 56405034493 minus 51539607552 gives 4865426941, and subtracting 4294967296 from that yields 570459645. Now continuing with the remaining characters, I'm processing 'e' and 's' through the same hash function, which gives me a final hash value of 2755266229, and I'm converting that to hexadecimal. Finishing the hex conversion with the remaining digits, then verifying the result by converting back to decimal to confirm it matches the original number.\n\nNow I'm formatting the hash as \"HDLmClassa43a06b5\" following the naming convention, and building out the full HTML page with a header, navigation, hero section, product showcase, and footer, incorporating the banner with the computed class name at the top.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I need to retrieve the URL first.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The fetched content was minimal, so I'm building out a complete HTML homepage structure that incorporates the limited text while adding the promotional banner as the main enhancement—a top banner advertising free shipping over $75 with a 15% discount code and Shop Now link. I'm also computing the DJB2 hash for tracking purposes.\n\nComputing DJB2 hash... Continuing through the hash computation with modular arithmetic, processing each character of the string and tracking the running hash value mod 2^32 as I work through the space and subsequent letters. Continuing through the hash calculations for the remaining characters, working through the modular arithmetic to track the running hash value as each character gets processed. Computing hash values through the string... Continuing the hash calculations for the remaining characters in \"offer\"... Continuing the hash calculations through the remaining characters, working through the modulo operations to keep the values in range. Continuing the hash computation through the remaining characters of \"happing love\", tracking the modulo operations at each step to keep the values within bounds. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters in \"rand \", tracking the modular arithmetic at each step to keep the hash value within bounds. Continuing through the hash calculations for the remaining characters in \"a1 5% dis co\", tracking the modulo operations as the hash values cycle through the 32-bit range. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters: c, o, d, e, and another space, applying the same modular arithmetic pattern to update the hash value at each step. Continuing the hash computation through the remaining characters of \"Shop a\" by applying the same polynomial rolling hash algorithm with modular arithmetic. Continuing through the hash calculations for the remaining characters in \"link\", then moving on to analyze the \"Why\" string about promotional strategies and their impact on conversion metrics. Continuing the hash calculations through the remaining characters of \"promotion\" to verify the final hash value. Continuing the hash computation through the remaining characters of \"banner s\", processing each letter through the polynomial rolling hash algorithm with modular arithmetic to track the intermediate values. Continuing the hash calculations through the remaining characters of the string. Computing the hash value for the space character and continuing through the remaining characters, accounting for the 32-bit overflow when the intermediate result exceeds the maximum value. Continuing the hash computation through the remaining characters of the string, processing each letter and applying the modulo operations to keep the values within bounds. Continuing to work through the hash computation, I'm verifying each character's contribution to the running hash value, carefully handling the modulo arithmetic to keep the values in range. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters in \"increaseS\" — working through each letter with the rolling hash algorithm, applying modulo operations to keep values within bounds. Continuing the hash calculations... Continuing the hash computation... Continuing the hash computation... Continuing the hash computation... Continuing the hash computation through the remaining characters of \"hates by cr\"... Computing hash values... Continuing through the hash calculations for the remaining characters in \"and ince\"... Continuing the hash computation... I need to recalculate that last step—I made an error with the modulo arithmetic. Let me redo it: 56405034493 minus 51539607552 gives 4865426941, and subtracting 4294967296 from that yields 570459645. Now continuing with the remaining characters, I'm processing 'e' and 's' through the same hash function, which gives me a final hash value of 2755266229, and I'm converting that to hexadecimal. Finishing the hex conversion with the remaining digits, then verifying the result by converting back to decimal to confirm it matches the original number.\n\nNow I'm formatting the hash as \"HDLmClassa43a06b5\" following the naming convention, and building out the full HTML page with a header, navigation, hero section, product showcase, and footer, incorporating the banner with the computed class name at the top.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":1,"signature":""}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":4016,"completion_tokens":17632,"total_tokens":21648,"cost":0.92176,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.92176,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.04016,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.8816},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1100,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0},"server_tool_use_details":{"web_search_requests":0}}}
